given cmp_fixture ((import bin_eq), "words", "want"):() then prints:("<stdin>:1: error: '2 == 5' mixes words; parenthesize it as the current precedence reads it: 'want' [E0601]\n  at: 2 == 5\n  why: the bitwise operators bind tighter than the comparisons in id and looser in C, so a reader who knows the other table reads the line differently; the rule asks for the grouping to be written down\n  help: write the parentheses the current precedence implies\n  edit: machine\treplace\t1\t2 == 5\twant\n")

mixed_fix(int id) {
  int i1_of_v = (import ni1)[id];
  int i2_of_v = (import ni2)[id];
  string ret_s = fix_side(id, i1_of_v) + " " + (import ns1)[id] + " " + fix_side(id, i2_of_v);
} return string ret_s;
given cmp_fixture ((import bin_mixed)):("(2 & 5) < 2")
